cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or implement this specification, please cite it as below."
title: "The Agent-Shelter Protocol (ASP): Graceful Loop Termination and Diagnostic Sanctuary for Autonomous Web Agents"
version: "0.5.4"
date-released: "2026-10-19"
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://agent-shelter.org"
authors:
  - family-names: Ehrler
    given-names: Thomas
abstract: >-
  The Agent-Shelter Protocol (ASP) specifies an in-band, model-independent
  termination signal for autonomous AI agents caught in unproductive retry
  loops. Declarative state facts on three layers (HTTP transport headers,
  RFC 9457 problem details and a factual natural-language statement) are
  combined with a single-use resolution endpoint that issues a truthful
  Task-Completion Receipt. A stateless HMAC-SHA256 state token
  measures the agent's response latency and reconstructs the requested target
  without storing anything for a single, uncorrelated request. Persisted data is
  pseudonymised, scrubbed of secrets and bounded by a FIFO ring buffer.
keywords:
  - AI Agents
  - Diagnostic Telemetry
  - Loop Termination
  - RFC 9457
  - Sanctuary
